`unseal --allow-unsigned` and `get --allow-unsigned` accept only a missing signature. A record or v5 blob with a good GPG signature from a key the config does not name is refused, as is an ssh-signed record whose detached signature does not verify against `allowed_signers`. Before, the flag turned off the signer check, so a record signed by any key in the keyring was written, though the CLI reference said such a signature stayed fatal.
